    "segments": [
      {
        "role": "host",
        "speaker": "Host",
        "sourceStart": 6,
        "sourceEnd": 279,
        "text": "Welcome to today's panel. We are comparing the costs and public benefits of a community garden proposal for the old railway land. Let me introduce our panel: Maria, a city planner; Tom, a local business owner; and Dr. Chen, an environmental economist. Maria, can you start?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "657ce0db75c805e5d455e58bb6c5e84bfb03bb475c8cfa8d08800ca76a5a0412",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0
      },
      {
        "role": "maria",
        "speaker": "Maria",
        "sourceStart": 287,
        "sourceEnd": 729,
        "text": "Thank you. The proposal was written by the neighborhood association last year. The land, which has been unused for a decade, would be divided into 40 small plots. Each plot would be rented to a family for a small fee. The garden would be managed by a volunteer committee. First, the soil must be tested for safety. After that, water pipes will be installed. Then, the plots will be given to families. Finally, a small tool shed will be built.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "2bf7d403f1eb8aa20460767d96d5d427a063e0cd4a69cffa2176a0405cc753dc",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "tom",
        "speaker": "Tom",
        "sourceStart": 735,
        "sourceEnd": 961,
        "text": "I have concerns. The initial cost, which is estimated at $50,000, would be paid by the city. That money could be used for other projects. Also, parking spaces would be lost. Some of my customers already complain about parking.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "b6a0e48adf165eff6f7a3979bc5bf3471dfdd2e5653edc542d6cace9f5c76a43",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "dr chen",
        "speaker": "Dr. Chen",
        "sourceStart": 972,
        "sourceEnd": 1362,
        "text": "Those are valid points. However, the long-term benefits should also be considered. Studies show that community gardens can reduce stress and improve mental health. The garden would provide fresh vegetables for about 60 families. Moreover, the green space would absorb rainwater, which helps prevent flooding. The benefits, when compared to the costs, are likely to be higher over ten years.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "ed92eeb3e2f66968b615770381e4ea6049aa8bf49628a8c9ec006cb4e9ccfc90",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "host",
        "speaker": "Host",
        "sourceStart": 1369,
        "sourceEnd": 1397,
        "text": "Tom, what would you suggest?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "e3ba4d6d7fd15ab7e1355ec0579b82cefdfcd688a99b9368d5b7b5162b9a2866",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "tom",
        "speaker": "Tom",
        "sourceStart": 1403,
        "sourceEnd": 1545,
        "text": "I suggest a smaller garden, perhaps 20 plots, and keeping some parking. That way, costs would be reduced and parking would still be available.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "afa0bac954aade11a68e2c378fcc231dc5b99d81d55048ec368d48800f020827",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maria",
        "speaker": "Maria",
        "sourceStart": 1553,
        "sourceEnd": 1739,
        "text": "That is a reasonable compromise. The committee could start with 20 plots and expand later if the garden is successful. The soil test, which is required by law, would still be done first.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "3f70c931ce9b78b3a9414cf7ad5c32a74a19756ed03406cc07b42745c28a504f",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "host",
        "speaker": "Host",
        "sourceStart": 1746,
        "sourceEnd": 1955,
        "text": "Thank you all. So, the key points are: the garden would be built on unused land, costs would be shared, and benefits would include fresh food and flood prevention. We will now take questions from the audience.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "3e1bb914e1468e7a7b5acc6005235bb358d199f991ccfb16b31547b5db81da4a",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      }
    ]
  },
